From: Armbian <info@armbian.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/meson: TranSwitch HDMI: limit to 8 bpc

On the MXQ (S805) the 7.2 kernel sets up 1080p60 with the right clocks
(TMDS 1485 MHz, pixel 148.5 MHz) and the sink detects the signal, but
the screen stays black, even with the VENC test pattern and the
TranSwitch BIST. A register dump against 6.12, which shows a picture on
the same box and monitor, differs in TX_VIDEO_DTV_MODE and
TX_VIDEO_DTV_OPTION_L: 7.2 programs 30-bit (10 bpc) output, 6.12 24-bit.

The HDMI state helper now picks the highest bpc the sink supports, up to
bridge.max_bpc (12 here), but the Meson8/8b video clock tree leaves the
TMDS clock at the 8 bpc rate. Limit the bridge to 8 bpc.

Signed-off-by: Armbian <info@armbian.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/meson/meson_transwitch_hdmi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/meson/meson_transwitch_hdmi.c
index f33f27f..6fada86 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/meson/meson_transwitch_hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/meson/meson_transwitch_hdmi.c
@@ -1354,7 +1354,13 @@ static int meson_txc_hdmi_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 			   DRM_BRIDGE_OP_HDMI | DRM_BRIDGE_OP_HDMI_AUDIO;
 	priv->bridge.type = DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_HDMIA;
 	priv->bridge.interlace_allowed = true;
-	priv->bridge.max_bpc = 12;
+	/*
+	 * The Meson8/8b video clock tree does not scale the TMDS clock for
+	 * deep colour, so anything above 8 bpc is packed into an 8 bpc TMDS
+	 * clock and the sink shows nothing.  Since 7.2 the HDMI state helper
+	 * picks the highest bpc the sink supports, up to this limit.
+	 */
+	priv->bridge.max_bpc = 8;
 	priv->bridge.supported_formats = BIT(DRM_OUTPUT_COLOR_FORMAT_RGB444) |
 					 BIT(DRM_OUTPUT_COLOR_FORMAT_YCBCR422) |
 					 BIT(DRM_OUTPUT_COLOR_FORMAT_YCBCR444);
